WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:00.903
- How was your dad?

00:00:00.903 --> 00:00:01.790
What made him a great dad?

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:04.040
'Cause he had to of
been really busy, right?

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:04.873
- You know what,

00:00:04.873 --> 00:00:08.340
he was very present.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.860
And, he figured out,

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.620
my parents, together, figured out,

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.750
given their life situation,
how to be present.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.650
And it looks different
for every single family.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:22.263
Everyone has a lot of plates
that they're spinning,

00:00:22.263 --> 00:00:25.250
and it's different for every individual.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.560
And so, what that looked like,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.860
in terms of my childhood
was we were just traveling.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:34.130
My mom would figure it
out so that all four kids,

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.100
we could go wherever my dad was going.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.810
And we would enroll in local schools,

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:40.370
or get homeschooled, and--

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.390
- Wow, it's almost like touring musicians.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:43.223
It's almost like how,

00:00:43.223 --> 00:00:45.730
'cause a lot of musicians
bring their kids on the road,

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:46.970
and families on the road.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:49.367
- Yes, that's exactly, exactly it,

00:00:49.367 --> 00:00:51.770
and it was awesome, because I loved it.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:54.470
And my parents figured out pretty early,

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:56.290
that they could really control me

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:57.260
by threatening that I wouldn't

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.091
be allowed to go to
set if I didn't behave.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:00.490
(laughing)

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:02.973
- I'm not above bribery
or threatening, myself.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.301
No, I think that's cool.
- And so, that happened, yeah.

00:01:06.301 --> 00:01:07.559
- Yeah.

00:01:07.559 --> 00:01:09.783
Well, I have a little surprise for you.

00:01:09.783 --> 00:01:10.616
- Oh, do you?

00:01:10.616 --> 00:01:12.472
- I have a Father's Day surprise for you.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:13.740
- [Bryce] Of Father's Day?

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.920
- Yes, a video was sent
to us just for you.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:16.760
Here, here we go.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:17.760
We're gonna play it.

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:20.000
- Hey, Kelly, well let's see,

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.020
an embarrassing story about Bryce.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.610
Well, she was a great kid,

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:26.020
and she loved visiting the set,

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:27.890
and she was very, very helpful.

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.660
In fact, by the time she was 11 or 12,

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:35.410
she was actually pitching in
as a production assistant.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:39.840
In fact, she was so efficient
that she was finally

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.530
given the responsibility
of having a walkie-talkie,

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:46.100
so that the production assistants
could talk to one another

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.470
and give direction and guidance,

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:52.234
and I mean that was a
real honor and a show

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:56.370
of appreciation for how
much or who she was.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.420
It was great.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.060
The first day, she was
terrific, she was on it.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.770
The second day was good too,

00:02:01.770 --> 00:02:03.660
except suddenly over the walkie-talkie,

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:08.660
we heard Bryce ordering
the extras holding area

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:13.110
to be moved from one side of
a building over to the other.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.690
Now, granted she was trying
to get it out of the sun

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.240
and into the shade,

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.330
and her thinking was pretty good,

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.200
but it's not quite cool
to have the 12-year-old

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.780
taking over the production.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:26.280
So she lost her walkie-talkie that day,

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:27.850
but I knew that one day,

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.620
she'd wanna be behind the
scenes calling the shots,

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.020
and she does it really well.

